From 5611e72707c4803bc58ad94510a852d9a6363ea5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jjohare <github@thedreamlab.uk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:02:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core,syntax): compute on stored values, not on the print
 format

Procedures read numeric cells through `DataSet::get_cell_display` and parsed the formatted string
back to f64. Numeric CSV columns get a two-decimal print format, so every procedure computed on
values rounded to 2 dp (0.123456 was read as 0.12). As in SPSS, a print format governs display
only.

Add `DataSet::get_cell_numeric`, which returns the stored value with the same missing-value
handling (Null, empty, ".", "NA"), and use it at the 30 sites that parsed the display string as a
number (DESCRIPTIVES, REGRESSION, CORRELATIONS, PARTIAL CORR, t-tests, ANOVA, GLM, nonparametric,
FACTOR, RELIABILITY, CURVEFIT, logistic and multinomial regression, MEANS, SELECT IF). Sites that
use the display string as a group key or to match text are unchanged.

Tests: numeric_precision_tests.rs on exactly linear data (y = 2x + 0.001, three decimals): mean,
slope, intercept and r are exact to 1e-9; three of the four fail before this change.

Co-Authored-By: jjohare <github@thedreamlab.uk>
